# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/classes.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event pyro_candle
# en: Light the Candle
title [b66d59] = 点燃蜡烛
# en: Professor Thorne places a candle at the far end of the hall. "Light it. From there." The class holds its breath. Last week a boy lit his own sleeve.
text [249ae3] = 索恩教授把一支蜡烛放在大厅的尽头。“点燃它。就站在那儿。”全班屏住了呼吸。上周有个男生点着了自己的袖子。
# en: A dark classroom, a single candle on a stool at the far end, Professor Thorne's silhouette with folded arms.
scene [b8447a] = 昏暗的教室，远处凳子上立着一支蜡烛，索恩教授抱着双臂的剪影。
# en: A careful spark
opt.left.label [1455cd] = 一点小心的火花
# en: The wick catches with a polite little flame. Thorne grunts. From him, that is applause.
opt.left.say.1 [e34a27] = 烛芯燃起一朵彬彬有礼的小火苗。索恩哼了一声。从他嘴里出来，这就算掌声了。
# en: Nothing. Then a wisp of smoke from your fingertips. A few people giggle.
opt.left.say.2 [266366] = 什么也没有。然后你的指尖冒出一缕青烟。几个人咯咯笑了起来。
# en: Show them real fire
opt.right.label [c2dc32] = 让他们见识真正的火
# en: The candle erupts in a pillar of white flame and then settles, obedient. The room goes quiet.
opt.right.say.1 [d02a9d] = 蜡烛喷出一道白色火柱，随即乖乖地平息下来。教室里鸦雀无声。
# en: The candle lights. So do the curtains. And, briefly, your eyebrows.
opt.right.say.2 [ed4c08] = 蜡烛点着了。窗帘也点着了。还有——短暂地——你的眉毛。

@event pyro_ember_heart
# en: The Ember Within
title [819842] = 心中余烬
# en: Today's exercise: hold a spark inside your chest and let it grow. "Fire is fed by will," says Thorne. "And by you, if you are careless." It burns. It is supposed to burn.
text [9171f7] = 今天的练习：把一点火星含在胸中，让它慢慢长大。“火以意志为食，”索恩说，“如果你不小心，也以你为食。”很烫。本来就该烫。
# en: Students sitting cross-legged in a stone circle, each with a faint glow behind their ribs.
scene [c54174] = 学生们盘腿坐在石圈里，每个人的肋骨后都透出微弱的光。
# en: Stop when it hurts
opt.left.label [d5afc2] = 痛了就停
# en: You let the spark gutter out. Thorne says nothing. The silence is a grade.
opt.left.say.1 [189b77] = 你让火星熄灭了。索恩一言不发。这份沉默就是分数。
# en: Hold it longer than anyone
opt.right.label [a7c8d5] = 坚持得比谁都久
# en: Your vision goes white at the edges. When you open your eyes, your breath is steaming and the stones around you are warm.
opt.right.say.1 [4859e1] = 你的视野边缘泛起一片白。睁开眼时，你呼出的气在冒白烟，周围的石头都是温热的。

@event pyro_lyra_spar
# en: A Challenge in Class
title [68aa64] = 课堂上的挑战
# en: "Professor, I'd like a demonstration partner." Lyra Vaneshade points her wand at you without looking. "That one."
text [c4c320] = “教授，我想要一个演示搭档。”莱拉·凡妮希德看都没看，就把魔杖指向了你。“就那个。”
# en: Two students facing each other across a scorched practice ring; one is a tall girl with crimson hair, flames curling around her wrists.
scene [377b0a] = 两名学生隔着烧焦的练习圈对峙；其中一个是高挑的红发女孩，火焰缠绕在她的手腕上。
# en: Politely decline
opt.left.label [8a601d] = 礼貌地拒绝
# en: "As expected," Lyra says, and turns away. It stings worse than a burn would.
opt.left.say.1 [6071b1] = “果然。”莱拉说完便转过身去。这比被火烫还疼。
# en: Step into the ring
opt.right.label [bf566a] = 走进圈内
# en: Your fire meets hers and holds. When Thorne calls time, Lyra is breathing hard. "Again. Next week," she says.
opt.right.say.1 [4d681f] = 你的火焰迎上她的，稳稳顶住。索恩喊停时，莱拉气喘吁吁。“再来。下周。”她说。
# en: She wins in under a minute — but she looks at you afterwards like she's filing you away for later.
opt.right.say.2 [ab3e00] = 她不到一分钟就赢了——但她事后看你的眼神，像是把你归档留待日后处理。

@event tide_lake_lesson
# en: The Lake Answers
title [146cec] = 湖水的回应
# en: Waist-deep in the freezing lake at dawn, Professor Marisol tells you to ask the water to rise. "Ask," she says. "Never demand. The lake remembers rudeness."
text [781568] = 黎明时分，你站在齐腰深的冰冷湖水里，玛丽索尔教授让你请求湖水升起。“是请求，”她说，“永远别命令。湖会记仇。”
# en: Students standing waist-deep in a silver lake at dawn, ripples spiralling out from their outstretched hands.
scene [398563] = 黎明时分，学生们站在齐腰深的银色湖水中，涟漪从他们伸出的手掌间旋转着荡开。
# en: Command it anyway
opt.left.label [400388] = 偏要命令它
# en: The water rises in a shivering column. Marisol raises an eyebrow. "Effective. Rude."
opt.left.say.1 [4cfa1b] = 湖水升起一道颤抖的水柱。玛丽索尔挑了挑眉。“有效。无礼。”
# en: The lake declines, and expresses its displeasure by knocking you flat.
opt.left.say.2 [412991] = 湖拒绝了，并用一个浪头把你拍倒来表达不满。
# en: Listen first
opt.right.label [c35e18] = 先倾听
# en: You stand still until the cold stops hurting. The lake murmurs — and for a moment you could swear it said your name.
opt.right.say.1 [17e74d] = 你一动不动，直到寒冷不再刺痛。湖水低声絮语——有一瞬间，你敢发誓它叫了你的名字。

@event tide_storm_drill
# en: Storm Drill
title [cb32cb] = 风暴演练
# en: A storm rolls over the lake and Marisol is delighted. "Perfect conditions! Hold back the rain for as long as you can." Most of the class has already fled.
text [1b19ce] = 一场风暴卷过湖面，玛丽索尔高兴坏了。“完美的条件！尽可能久地挡住雨！”班上大部分人早已逃之夭夭。
# en: A rocky shore under black clouds, a few figures in soaked robes holding back a curtain of rain with raised hands.
scene [04bfa1] = 乌云下的岩石湖岸，几个浑身湿透的身影举起双手，挡住一道雨幕。
# en: Shelter with the sensible ones
opt.left.label [897439] = 和明智的人一起躲雨
# en: You watch from the boathouse, dry and slightly ashamed.
opt.left.say.1 [061ff3] = 你在船屋里观看，身上干爽，心里略感惭愧。
# en: Stay out in it
opt.right.label [f1db6c] = 留在雨里
# en: You hold the rain back for almost a minute. You also catch Lake Fever.
opt.right.say.1 [28d2b9] = 你挡住雨将近一分钟。你也染上了湖热病。
# en: For a full minute, the rain parts around you. Marisol whoops like a child.
opt.right.say.2 [814a26] = 整整一分钟，雨水在你周围分开。玛丽索尔像个孩子一样欢呼。

@event tide_drowned_bell
# en: The Drowned Bell
title [5e6210] = 沉没的钟
# en: Ever since the lake held its breath in Mistveil, you listen for it. During a breathing-charm lesson you hear it: a bell, deep under the lake, tolling slow and soft. Nobody else seems to notice.
text [c76f61] = 自从迷雾月湖水屏住呼吸之后，你就一直在留意。在一堂水下呼吸咒的课上，你听见了：湖底深处有一口钟，缓慢而轻柔地敲响。似乎没有别人注意到。
# en: Murky green water, a shaft of light catching the bronze curve of an enormous bell half-buried in silt.
scene [7fdf05] = 浑浊的绿色湖水中，一束光照亮了一口半埋在淤泥里的巨钟的青铜弧面。
# en: Mention it to Professor Marisol
opt.left.label [dfb6fd] = 告诉玛丽索尔教授
# en: Her face goes very still. "There is no bell," she says. "There hasn't been a bell for three hundred years."
opt.left.say.1 [084e01] = 她的表情一下子僵住了。“没有什么钟，”她说，“三百年来，那里都没有钟。”
# en: Dive down to find it
opt.right.label [86c496] = 潜下去找它
# en: Deep in the silt you find a broken piece of bronze, warm to the touch, engraved with a black star.
opt.right.say.1 [6a378c] = 在深深的淤泥里，你找到一块破碎的青铜，摸上去是温的，上面刻着一颗黑色的星。
# en: The water closes over you, dark and cold. You surface gasping, empty-handed, with the bell still ringing in your teeth.
opt.right.say.2 [d6f863] = 湖水在你头顶合拢，黑暗而冰冷。你两手空空地浮上水面，大口喘气，那钟声还在你牙齿间回荡。

@event illusion_mirror_self
# en: A Second You
title [77533b] = 另一个你
# en: Assignment: conjure a convincing illusion of yourself. Professor Vey circles the room. "Most students make themselves taller. Interesting, what people choose."
text [a41437] = 作业：变出一个以假乱真的自己。维伊教授在教室里踱步。“大多数学生会把自己变高一点。人们的选择，真有意思。”
# en: A student facing a shimmering duplicate of themselves; the duplicate's smile is a little too wide.
scene [a36cd8] = 一个学生面对着自己闪闪发光的分身；分身的笑容咧得有点太开了。
# en: Make it flattering
opt.left.label [90461e] = 美化一下
# en: Your double is radiant, confident, slightly better-looking. Vey writes something down and smiles thinly.
opt.left.say.1 [07e402] = 你的分身容光焕发、自信满满，长得还比你好看一点。维伊记下了什么，淡淡一笑。
# en: Make it accurate
opt.right.label [a663ce] = 如实呈现
# en: Your double slouches the way you slouch and chews its lip the way you do. It is deeply unsettling. Vey awards top marks.
opt.right.say.1 [6dfcc6] = 你的分身和你一样驼着背，和你一样咬着嘴唇。这让人非常不安。维伊给了满分。

@event illusion_professor_prank
# en: The Professor's Face
title [795234] = 教授的脸
# en: Your classmates dare you: wear a glamour of Professor Thorne and cancel tomorrow's Arcana lecture. "Nobody will know," says someone who will definitely tell.
text [f7081e] = 同学们怂恿你：用幻术变成索恩教授的模样，取消明天的奥术课。“没人会发现的。”说这话的人一定会去告密。
# en: A student wearing a shimmering glamour of a stern old professor, classmates stifling laughter behind a door.
scene [6c7f98] = 一个学生顶着严厉老教授的闪烁幻象，同学们躲在门后憋着笑。
# en: Absolutely not
opt.left.label [c1af76] = 绝对不行
# en: Wise. Someone else tries it the next day and spends a week scrubbing gargoyles.
opt.left.say.1 [2654ad] = 明智。第二天另一个人试了，结果刷了一个星期的石像鬼。
# en: Do it
opt.right.label [f29ea1] = 干了
# en: "Class is cancelled," you announce in Thorne's gravel voice. The cheering is audible from three towers away.
opt.right.say.1 [52cb62] = “今天停课。”你用索恩那砂砾般的嗓音宣布。欢呼声在三座塔外都听得见。
# en: Halfway through, the glamour flickers. The real Thorne is standing in the doorway. He is not laughing.
opt.right.say.2 [c3574a] = 演到一半，幻术闪了一下。真正的索恩就站在门口。他没有笑。

@event illusion_dragon
# en: The Courtyard Dragon
title [e608ce] = 庭院里的龙
# en: For your term project you must create an illusion that fools a crowd. You could make something small and flawless. Or you could put a dragon in the courtyard at lunchtime.
text [47084a] = 你的学期作业是制造一个能骗过一群人的幻象。你可以做个小而完美的东西。或者，你可以在午饭时间往庭院里放一条龙。
# en: A vast translucent dragon coiled around the academy's central fountain, students frozen mid-step beneath it.
scene [56332c] = 一条巨大的半透明的龙盘绕在学院中央喷泉上，下方的学生们僵在原地。
# en: Small and flawless
opt.left.label [1a8234] = 小而完美
# en: A single butterfly that nobody can tell is fake. Vey taps it with her wand and it bursts into light. "Perfect."
opt.left.say.1 [b8332b] = 一只谁也看不出是假的蝴蝶。维伊用魔杖轻轻一点，它化作一团光。“完美。”
# en: Dragon. Obviously.
opt.right.label [602404] = 龙。当然是龙。
# en: The dragon uncurls around the fountain and yawns. Forty students scream. Vey laughs until she cries.
opt.right.say.1 [617c57] = 龙绕着喷泉舒展身体，打了个哈欠。四十个学生尖叫起来。维伊笑得眼泪都出来了。
# en: The dragon is magnificent for four seconds and then sneezes into a cloud of glitter. The headmistress was eating lunch below it.
opt.right.say.2 [f1e819] = 那条龙壮观了四秒钟，然后打了个喷嚏，化作一团亮片。院长当时正在下面吃午饭。

@event alch_first_brew
# en: Draught of Mild Courage
title [da711f] = 微勇药剂
# en: The recipe is on the board: Draught of Mild Courage. Seven ingredients, three stirs clockwise, one counter-clockwise, and never — never — add the newt eye early.
text [74f236] = 配方写在黑板上：微勇药剂。七种原料，顺时针搅三下，逆时针一下，而且绝不——绝不——能提前放蝾螈眼。
# en: Rows of bubbling cauldrons in a low stone room, each giving off a different coloured steam.
scene [88ce92] = 低矮的石室里一排排冒泡的坩埚，每一口都升起不同颜色的蒸汽。
# en: Follow the recipe exactly
opt.left.label [ae651f] = 严格按配方来
# en: A clear, honey-coloured brew. The professor sniffs it and nods. Safe, solid, unremarkable.
opt.left.say.1 [6cc5ac] = 一锅清澈的蜂蜜色药剂。教授闻了闻，点点头。安全、扎实、平平无奇。
# en: Improvise a little
opt.right.label [99aea4] = 稍微即兴发挥
# en: Your variant tastes like cinnamon and makes people brave enough to ask for things. A fourth-year buys the whole flask.
opt.right.say.1 [228a65] = 你的改良版尝起来有肉桂味，能让人鼓起勇气开口要东西。一个四年级生把整瓶都买走了。
# en: You taste-test. Mistake. For the next month, everything you say comes out as a deep, wet croak.
opt.right.say.2 [875ffe] = 你亲口尝了一下。失误。接下来一个月，你说的每句话都变成了低沉潮湿的呱呱声。

@event alch_unstable_cauldron
# en: Unstable Cauldron
title [69d2ed] = 不稳定的坩埚
# en: The cauldron next to yours starts to shudder. Its owner, a terrified first-year, has added the newt eye early. It is going to blow.
text [e609c0] = 你旁边的坩埚开始颤抖。它的主人，一个吓坏了的一年级生，提前放了蝾螈眼。它要炸了。
# en: A cauldron shuddering on its iron legs, violet bubbles swelling over the rim, a student frozen beside it.
scene [444a20] = 一口坩埚在铁脚上颤动，紫色气泡从锅沿鼓出，旁边的学生僵住了。
# en: Dive for cover
opt.left.label [5f718b] = 扑倒找掩护
# en: The explosion paints the ceiling violet. Nobody is hurt. Everybody is purple.
opt.left.say.1 [c25dd0] = 爆炸把天花板染成了紫色。没人受伤。所有人都变紫了。
# en: Try to neutralise it
opt.right.label [cd26e0] = 试着中和它
# en: A pinch of salt, a drop of moonwater, a quick counter-stir. The bubbling dies. The first-year bursts into grateful tears.
opt.right.say.1 [21799b] = 一撮盐，一滴月光水，飞快地反向搅动。冒泡停了。那个一年级生感激得哭了出来。
# en: The cauldron goes off in your face. You spend a week with violet eyebrows and a ringing in your ears.
opt.right.say.2 [2f0478] = 坩埚在你脸上炸开了。你顶着紫色眉毛、耳朵嗡嗡响地过了一个星期。

@event alch_corvin_market
# en: A Side Business
title [5b5ae3] = 副业
# en: Corvin turns your leftover potions over in his hands. "These would sell for real crowns in the village. I know a buyer. I take a third. Nobody needs to know they came from a classroom."
text [179554] = 科尔文把你剩下的药剂在手里翻来覆去地看。“这些在镇上能卖真金白银。我认识个买家。我抽三成。没人需要知道它们是从教室里出来的。”
# en: A young man leaning on a cauldron table, holding up a vial against the light with a merchant's grin.
scene [95a8de] = 一个年轻人倚着坩埚桌，把一只小瓶举到光下，脸上挂着商人的笑。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: "Your loss, saint." He tosses the vial back. You fumble it.
opt.left.say.1 [160723] = “你的损失，圣人。”他把小瓶扔回来。你手忙脚乱地接住。
# en: Shake on it
opt.right.label [982713] = 一言为定
# en: It goes well until a vial turns up in a professor's tea. You and Corvin share a detention and an alibi.
opt.right.say.1 [f97a4d] = 一切顺利，直到一只小瓶出现在某位教授的茶里。你和科尔文共享了一次禁闭和一份不在场证明。
# en: Thirty crowns, no questions asked. Corvin winks. "Pleasure doing crime with you."
opt.right.say.2 [d740ff] = 三十克朗，不问来路。科尔文眨眨眼。“和你一起犯罪真愉快。”

@event div_tea_leaves
# en: Reading the Leaves
title [0b5484] = 解读茶叶
# en: You read your partner's tea leaves. The shape at the bottom of the cup is unmistakably a skull. Your partner is looking at you hopefully.
text [724f94] = 你为搭档解读茶叶。杯底的形状明明白白是一个骷髅。你的搭档满怀希望地看着你。
# en: A delicate teacup tipped on its saucer, the dregs forming a shape like a skull — or possibly a mushroom.
scene [006d77] = 一只精致的茶杯倾倒在茶碟上，杯底的残渣形如骷髅——也可能是蘑菇。
# en: Tell the truth
opt.left.label [d8bf00] = 说实话
# en: "A skull?" They laugh. "Professor says a skull means change." They're relieved. You aren't sure you should be.
opt.left.say.1 [fd9f44] = “骷髅？”对方笑了，“教授说骷髅代表改变。”对方松了口气。你却不确定该不该松这口气。
# en: They go pale and leave early. The next day they trip down the stairs. Nothing serious. Still.
opt.left.say.2 [e9a649] = 对方脸色煞白，提前离开了。第二天对方从楼梯上摔了一跤。不严重。但还是。
# en: Lie kindly
opt.right.label [542b7a] = 善意地撒谎
# en: "A mushroom," you say. "Means good fortune." They beam. The professor, passing behind you, says nothing at all.
opt.right.say.1 [739452] = “是蘑菇，”你说，“代表好运。”对方笑开了花。从你身后走过的教授什么也没说。
# en: Foretell what it really means
opt.up.label [ce137c] = 预言它真正的含义
# en: You say, out loud and quite certain, that the skull means your partner will lose a bet before Friday. They lose a bet on Thursday, to you, and are thrilled the skull wasn't worse.
opt.up.say.1 [c2eccc] = 你笃定地大声说，那个骷髅的意思是你的搭档周五前会输掉一个赌。周四他就输了一个赌，输给了你，而且庆幸骷髅没意味着更糟的事。

@event div_next_tuesday
# en: The Mirror of Next Tuesday
title [765386] = 下周二之镜
# en: The Mirror of Next Tuesday shows exactly what it promises. Students take turns looking. Some come away smiling. One comes away and goes straight to the infirmary.
text [3591e5] = “下周二之镜”展示的正如其名。学生们轮流去看。有人笑着离开。有一个人看完直接去了医务室。
# en: An ornate standing mirror whose reflection shows the room on a different day — the light at a different angle, a different person sitting in your chair.
scene [abfe7b] = 一面华丽的落地镜，镜中映出的是另一天的这间屋子——光线角度不同，你的椅子上坐着别人。
# en: Take a look
opt.left.label [a3cf08] = 看一眼
# en: Next Tuesday you are sitting an Astromancy quiz. You memorise the questions. Is that cheating? It's at least ambiguous.
opt.left.say.1 [0a0d2f] = 下周二你在参加星象学小测。你记下了题目。这算作弊吗？至少说不清。
# en: Next Tuesday you are crying in the rain outside the observatory. You don't know why. You spend the week dreading it.
opt.left.say.2 [004b37] = 下周二你在天文台外的雨里哭泣。你不知道为什么。接下来一整周你都提心吊胆。
# en: Decline
opt.right.label [eaef39] = 不看了
# en: "I'd rather be surprised." The professor smiles as if you have passed a different test entirely.
opt.right.say.1 [18dfd0] = “我宁愿到时候再惊喜。”教授笑了，好像你通过了另一场完全不同的考试。

@event div_seraphine_vision
# en: She Grabs Your Hand
title [a002e6] = 她抓住了你的手
# en: In the middle of crystal-gazing, Seraphine Hale seizes your wrist. Her eyes have gone silver. "The door under the lake," she whispers. "Don't let him open it. Or do. I can't see which."
text [52e443] = 正凝视水晶球时，瑟拉芬·海尔一把抓住你的手腕。她的眼睛变成了银色。“湖下的门，”她低语，“别让他打开它。或者让他打开。我看不清是哪个。”
# en: A dreamy-eyed girl gripping a classmate's wrist across a table of crystal balls, her pupils wide and silver.
scene [bda6a7] = 一个眼神迷离的女孩隔着摆满水晶球的桌子抓住同学的手腕，瞳孔放大，泛着银光。
# en: Pull away
opt.left.label [1414c0] = 抽回手
# en: She blinks and lets go. "Sorry. That happens." She goes back to her crystal as if nothing occurred.
opt.left.say.1 [d082da] = 她眨了眨眼，松开了手。“抱歉。偶尔会这样。”她若无其事地继续看她的水晶球。
# en: Ask who she means
opt.right.label [301f4e] = 问她说的是谁
# en: "Someone cold," she says. "Someone kind." Then she shakes her head, smiles vaguely, and asks if you'd like a biscuit.
opt.right.say.1 [c004e1] = “一个冰冷的人，”她说，“一个温柔的人。”然后她摇摇头，迷迷糊糊地笑了笑，问你要不要来块饼干。

@event art_clockwork_beetle
# en: The Clockwork Beetle
title [8b7d56] = 发条甲虫
# en: Your project: a brass beetle that walks. The gears are in. The spring is wound. You could make it efficient, or you could give it a little personality.
text [982bd2] = 你的作业：一只会走路的黄铜甲虫。齿轮装好了。发条上紧了。你可以让它高效，也可以给它一点个性。
# en: A brass beetle the size of a fist on a workbench, tiny gears visible through its translucent wing-cases.
scene [3cbbcc] = 工作台上一只拳头大小的黄铜甲虫，透过半透明的鞘翅能看见细小的齿轮。
# en: Make it efficient
opt.left.label [b934bb] = 让它高效
# en: It walks in a perfect straight line until it hits a wall. Full marks.
opt.left.say.1 [2f4098] = 它沿着一条完美的直线前进，直到撞上墙。满分。
# en: Give it personality
opt.right.label [40ed9d] = 给它点个性
# en: It escapes during the presentation and lives in the walls for a month, occasionally stealing biscuits. It becomes a minor legend.
opt.right.say.1 [a6886f] = 它在展示时逃跑了，在墙里住了一个月，时不时偷块饼干。它成了一个小小的传说。
# en: It refuses to walk unless you compliment it. The professor is torn between marking you down and asking how you did it.
opt.right.say.2 [550353] = 除非你夸它，不然它就不肯走。教授在扣你分和问你怎么做到的之间左右为难。
# en: Animate it instead of winding it
opt.up.label [f9c01b] = 不上发条，直接活化
# en: You skip the spring and give the beetle a want instead: to find the warmest spot on the bench. It does, and sits there, content, and nothing in the class is wound tighter or happier.
opt.up.say.1 [cf2421] = 你跳过发条，给了甲虫一个念想：去找桌上最暖和的地方。它找到了，心满意足地待在那儿。全班没有哪只甲虫比它上得更紧、过得更开心。

@event art_mir_collab
# en: A Joint Project
title [7a3675] = 合作项目
# en: Mir Ten drops onto the bench beside you with a sketch of something that is either a self-stirring cauldron or a small war machine. "Partners? Your hands, my brain. Or the other way round. Both, actually."
text [687dbc] = 米尔·滕一屁股坐到你旁边的长凳上，拿着一张草图，上面画的东西要么是自动搅拌坩埚，要么是一台小型战争机器。“搭档吗？你的手，我的脑子。或者反过来。其实两样都要。”
# en: A cluttered workbench covered in tools, sketches and one smoking teapot; a grinning student with goggles pushed up into wild hair.
scene [455820] = 堆满工具和草图的工作台上还有一只冒烟的茶壶；一个咧嘴笑的学生把护目镜推到了蓬乱的头发上。
# en: Work alone
opt.left.label [e54a87] = 自己干
# en: "Fair," says Mir, with no hard feelings, and is immediately on fire. Not badly.
opt.left.say.1 [461fb1] = “公平。”米尔毫无芥蒂地说，随即就着了火。不算严重。
# en: Partner with Mir
opt.right.label [89e907] = 和米尔搭档
# en: The cauldron stirs itself, hums a tune and only threatens the professor once. Mir hugs you with oily hands.
opt.right.say.1 [51d7a9] = 坩埚自己搅拌，还哼着小曲，只威胁了教授一次。米尔用满是油污的手抱住了你。
# en: The prototype explodes. Mir laughs so hard they cry. "Again! We were so close!" You find you're laughing too.
opt.right.say.2 [48c576] = 原型机爆炸了。米尔笑得眼泪直流。“再来！我们差一点就成了！”你发现自己也在笑。
# en: Build it on the spot
opt.up.label [7c2686] = 当场拼出来
# en: You don't sketch it. You ask the bits what they want to be, and they become a cauldron that stirs and occasionally salutes. Mir makes a noise you've never heard a person make. "Partners," Mir says. "Forever. Probably."
opt.up.say.1 [2c7e08] = 你不画图。你问那些零件想变成什么，它们就变成了一口会自己搅拌、偶尔还会敬个礼的坩埚。米尔发出一种你从没听人发出过的声音。“搭档，”米尔说，“永远的。大概吧。”

@event art_enchanted_quill
# en: The Self-Writing Quill
title [0d291a] = 自动羽毛笔
# en: You've enchanted a quill to take dictation. It works beautifully. A thought occurs: what if it wrote your essays, too?
text [8d3e40] = 你给一支羽毛笔施了魔法，让它听写。效果好极了。你冒出一个念头：要是让它连论文也写了呢？
# en: A quill writing busily on its own over a sheaf of paper while its owner sleeps on folded arms.
scene [789717] = 一支羽毛笔在一沓纸上自己奋笔疾书，它的主人趴在胳膊上睡着了。
# en: Just use it for notes
opt.left.label [1cd0cf] = 只用它记笔记
# en: Your notes are flawless. Even the professor's jokes are transcribed, with a small marginal comment: "(not funny)."
opt.left.say.1 [04dda1] = 你的笔记无懈可击。连教授的笑话都记下来了，旁边还有一行小小的批注：“（不好笑）”。
# en: Let it write your essays
opt.right.label [904901] = 让它替你写论文
# en: Your essays arrive on time, in impeccable penmanship. A little too impeccable. Nobody notices. Yet.
opt.right.say.1 [fd9908] = 你的论文按时交上，字迹工整无比。工整得有点过分了。没人发现。暂时。
# en: The quill develops opinions and writes a scathing review of the professor. It signs your name.
opt.right.say.2 [7b012f] = 羽毛笔有了自己的主见，写了一篇痛批教授的檄文。署的是你的名字。

@event beast_griffon_chick
# en: Hatching Day
title [e94ec5] = 破壳日
# en: The griffon egg is cracking. Professor Brask whispers that the first face a chick sees, it trusts forever — or attacks forever. Hard to predict.
text [713b1c] = 狮鹫蛋正在裂开。布拉斯克教授低声说，雏鸟看见的第一张脸，它会永远信任——或者永远攻击。很难预料。
# en: A straw nest under a heat lamp, a cracked golden egg, and a damp fluffy griffon chick blinking at the world.
scene [561fcb] = 保温灯下的草窝里，一枚裂开的金蛋，一只湿漉漉、毛茸茸的狮鹫雏鸟正眨着眼打量世界。
# en: Hang back
opt.left.label [7bd914] = 往后站
# en: The chick sees Brask first and bites her. She seems delighted.
opt.left.say.1 [72d465] = 雏鸟第一眼看见了布拉斯克，咬了她一口。她看起来很开心。
# en: Offer your hand
opt.right.label [1f34dd] = 伸出手
# en: The chick peeps, nuzzles your palm and falls asleep. You are, apparently, its mother now.
opt.right.say.1 [dd4810] = 雏鸟啾啾叫着，蹭了蹭你的掌心，睡着了。看来，你现在是它妈妈了。
# en: It bites. Hard. Griffon beaks are sharper than they look, and they look extremely sharp.
opt.right.say.2 [96c90d] = 它咬了你。狠狠地。狮鹫的喙比看上去锋利，而它看上去就极其锋利。

@event beast_manticore
# en: The Manticore Is Loose
title [c92a9e] = 蝎尾狮跑出来了
# en: Someone left the manticore pen open. It's in the greenhouse, tail twitching, between you and the only exit.
text [1d8358] = 有人没关蝎尾狮的围栏。它在温室里，尾巴抽动着，正挡在你和唯一的出口之间。
# en: A shadowy lion-shape with a scorpion's tail prowling between the greenhouse benches, students pressed against the glass.
scene [5076e9] = 一个带着蝎尾的狮形黑影在温室长凳间徘徊，学生们紧贴着玻璃墙。
# en: Back away slowly
opt.left.label [b7e862] = 慢慢后退
# en: You edge out. Professor Brask arrives with a bucket of meat and a lullaby and the crisis is over in minutes.
opt.left.say.1 [92deb4] = 你一点点挪了出去。布拉斯克教授带着一桶肉和一首摇篮曲赶来，几分钟就平息了危机。
# en: Try to calm it
opt.right.label [469057] = 试着安抚它
# en: You hum the lullaby Brask taught you. The manticore yawns, sits, and lets you scratch behind its ear. The whole class saw.
opt.right.say.1 [3bf240] = 你哼起布拉斯克教的摇篮曲。蝎尾狮打了个哈欠，坐下来，让你挠它的耳后。全班都看见了。
# en: The manticore does not like your humming. The tail is quicker than you are.
opt.right.say.2 [422c18] = 蝎尾狮不喜欢你的哼唱。它的尾巴比你快。

@event beast_familiar_call
# en: Calling a Familiar
title [b91c9f] = 召唤魔宠
# en: Brask teaches the summoning circle. "It doesn't summon," she says. "It invites. Most of the time, nothing comes. That's fine. Familiars choose you."
text [3a2457] = 布拉斯克教授教你们召唤法阵。“它并不召唤，”她说，“它只是邀请。大多数时候什么也不会来。没关系。魔宠会自己选择你。”
# en: A circle of salt and candles in a forest clearing at dusk, shapes of small animals watching from the edge of the trees.
scene [e641a7] = 黄昏时林间空地上一圈盐和蜡烛，林边有小动物的身影在注视。
# en: Just watch the others
opt.left.label [4c0d66] = 只看别人做
# en: A first-year is chosen by a very large toad. The toad looks smug about it.
opt.left.say.1 [4d8722] = 一个一年级生被一只非常大的蟾蜍选中了。蟾蜍看起来很得意。
# en: Sit in the circle
opt.right.label [69d42b] = 坐进法阵
# en: Nothing comes. But for a long moment, something at the edge of the trees watches you with eyes like embers. Then it is gone.
opt.right.say.1 [9c9f2a] = 什么也没来。但有很长一段时间，林边有什么东西用余烬般的眼睛注视着你。然后它消失了。

@event astro_comet
# en: A New Comet
title [6445f6] = 新彗星
# en: A comet appears that isn't in any of the charts. The observatory is in uproar. Everyone wants to be the one to name it.
text [b8052f] = 一颗不在任何星图上的彗星出现了。天文台炸开了锅。人人都想当给它命名的那个人。
# en: An observatory dome open to the night, a long-tailed comet smeared across the sky, students crowded at the telescopes.
scene [9a815d] = 向夜空敞开的天文台穹顶，一颗长尾彗星划过天际，学生们挤在望远镜前。
# en: Sketch it carefully
opt.left.label [5702fd] = 仔细画下它
# en: Your drawing is lovely. Someone else's name goes on the comet. You keep the drawing.
opt.left.say.1 [605f74] = 你画得很美。彗星用了别人的名字。你留下了那幅画。
# en: Calculate its path
opt.right.label [e158e4] = 计算它的轨道
# en: Your math is right. The comet is named after you, or at least after a slight misspelling of you.
opt.right.say.1 [1b11c9] = 你算对了。彗星以你的名字命名——至少是你名字的一个小小的错误拼写。
# en: Your calculation suggests the comet will hit the academy on Thursday. It does not. You are teased about it for weeks.
opt.right.say.2 [0e494e] = 你的计算显示彗星将在周四撞上学院。它没有。你被取笑了好几个星期。

@event astro_kael_roof
# en: Up All Night
title [f8c2d5] = 彻夜未眠
# en: On your way to the morning lecture you find Kael alone on the observatory roof. He has been there all night. Frost has spread across the tiles around him. He is staring at a patch of sky where there are no stars at all.
text [d9607d] = 去上早课的路上，你发现凯尔独自坐在天文台屋顶上。他在那儿待了一整夜。他周围的瓦片上结满了霜。他盯着天上一块一颗星星也没有的地方。
# en: A young man in a fur coat sitting alone on the observatory roof, frost on the tiles around him, staring at one spot in the stars.
scene [4d08d9] = 一个穿毛皮大衣的年轻人独自坐在天文台屋顶，身旁瓦片结霜，凝视着星空中的某一点。
# en: Leave him be
opt.left.label [ce4663] = 别打扰他
# en: You go down to class. By evening there's a perfect circle of frost on the roof where he sat, and no Kael.
opt.left.say.1 [8f95a8] = 你下楼去上课了。到了傍晚，屋顶上他坐过的地方留下了一个完美的霜圈，凯尔却不见了。
# en: Sit beside him
opt.right.label [746969] = 坐到他身边
# en: "There," he says, pointing at the dark. "Can you see it? A star that eats light." You look for a long time. You think you can.
opt.right.say.1 [28b9f2] = “那里，”他指着黑暗说，“你看见了吗？一颗吞噬光的星。”你看了很久。你觉得你看见了。

@event astro_sleepless
# en: Sleepless Weeks
title [848700] = 无眠的几周
# en: Midnight lectures, dawn homework, morning classes. You have started seeing constellations in your porridge.
text [5695ef] = 午夜讲座，黎明作业，上午上课。你已经开始在粥里看见星座了。
# en: A student asleep on an open star atlas at a library desk, a guttering candle beside them, dawn light in the window.
scene [e3c887] = 一个学生趴在图书馆书桌上摊开的星图集上睡着了，蜡烛将熄，窗外透进晨光。
# en: Skip a few lectures
opt.left.label [659dd6] = 翘几节讲座
# en: You sleep for fourteen hours and wake up feeling like a person.
opt.left.say.1 [c5fbc8] = 你睡了十四个小时，醒来时终于觉得自己像个人了。
# en: Power through
opt.right.label [8bebcb] = 硬撑过去
# en: You learn the names of forty stars and forget the names of two friends. Temporarily.
opt.right.say.1 [a83f16] = 你记住了四十颗星星的名字，忘了两个朋友的名字。暂时的。

@event heal_first_patient
# en: Your First Patient
title [aad265] = 你的第一位病人
# en: A first-year stumbles into the practice ward with a wrist that bends the wrong way. Sister Amaranth is busy. The first-year looks at you with enormous, trusting eyes.
text [2614f1] = 一个一年级生跌跌撞撞地走进实习病房，手腕弯向了错误的方向。阿玛兰斯修女正忙着。那个一年级生用一双大大的、充满信任的眼睛看着你。
# en: A pale first-year sitting on an infirmary cot holding a wrist at a strange angle, a nervous student healer kneeling beside them.
scene [0b1ccb] = 一个脸色苍白的一年级生坐在医务室病床上，托着一只角度怪异的手腕，一位紧张的学生治疗师跪在旁边。
# en: Fetch Sister Amaranth
opt.left.label [0ebdc9] = 去叫阿玛兰斯修女
# en: Amaranth fixes it in seconds and nods at you. "Knowing your limits is the first lesson."
opt.left.say.1 [386b03] = 阿玛兰斯几秒钟就治好了，对你点点头。“知道自己的极限，是第一课。”
# en: Heal it yourself
opt.right.label [6b0949] = 自己来治
# en: The bone slides back with a soft click and a glow of warm light. The first-year tells everyone you're a genius.
opt.right.say.1 [b682dc] = 骨头轻轻咔哒一声归位，泛起一阵温暖的光。那个一年级生逢人便说你是天才。
# en: The wrist is now straight. The fingers, however, are pointing backwards. Amaranth sighs and fixes both.
opt.right.say.2 [2d4421] = 手腕是直了。可手指却朝后指着。阿玛兰斯叹了口气，两样都修好了。

@event heal_fever_ward
# en: Fever in the Village
title [3e73df] = 小镇里的热病
# en: Lake Fever is spreading through the village below the academy. Sister Amaranth asks for student volunteers. It's hard, unpaid, and you might catch it.
text [ea106a] = 湖热病正在学院山下的小镇蔓延。阿玛兰斯修女在征集学生志愿者。辛苦、没报酬，你还可能被传染。
# en: A crowded village hall lined with cots, lanterns hanging from the rafters, student healers moving between patients.
scene [945032] = 一间摆满病床的拥挤镇公所，椽子上挂着灯笼，学生治疗师们在病人之间穿梭。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: You watch the volunteers board the barge in the morning. You do your homework. It feels like the wrong homework.
opt.left.say.1 [70c215] = 早上，你看着志愿者们登上驳船。你做着你的作业。感觉像是在做错的作业。
# en: Volunteer
opt.right.label [39a371] = 报名志愿
# en: You save lives, and catch the fever yourself. The village sends a basket of honey cakes to your sickbed.
opt.right.say.1 [d1e957] = 你救了人，自己也染上了热病。镇上送了一篮蜂蜜蛋糕到你的病床边。
# en: A week of long nights and cool cloths. When you leave, the baker's daughter gives you her best loaf.
opt.right.say.2 [61b0a3] = 一个星期的漫漫长夜和凉毛巾。你离开时，面包师的女儿送了你她烤得最好的一条面包。

@event heal_tobias_sting
# en: Stung
title [1eecd2] = 被蛰了
# en: Tobias wanders into the practice ward holding up a hand swollen like a pumpkin. "Mandrake," he says. "She didn't like my singing." He looks hopefully at you.
text [91e6f0] = 托比亚斯晃进实习病房，举着一只肿得像南瓜的手。“曼德拉草，”他说，“她不喜欢我唱歌。”他满怀希望地看着你。
# en: A broad-shouldered boy sitting on a greenhouse bench, grimacing, holding up a hand swollen to twice its size.
scene [37ac94] = 一个宽肩膀的男生坐在温室长凳上，龇牙咧嘴，举着一只肿成两倍大的手。
# en: Send him to the infirmary
opt.left.label [d6e106] = 让他去医务室
# en: "Right. Proper healer. Good idea." He goes, a little disappointed.
opt.left.say.1 [d77544] = “对。找正经治疗师。好主意。”他走了，有点失望。
# en: Treat him yourself
opt.right.label [2aa3de] = 亲自为他治疗
# en: Your hands are steady. The swelling goes down. Tobias stares at his hand, then at you. "You're really good at this," he says softly.
opt.right.say.1 [eb2831] = 你的手很稳。肿消了下去。托比亚斯盯着自己的手，又盯着你。“你真的很擅长这个。”他轻声说。

@event umbral_whisper
# en: The Shadow Speaks
title [041067] = 影子开口了
# en: In the middle of a lecture on the Nature of Absence, your shadow leans away from the lamp, toward your ear, and says your name.
text [a8a6b1] = 在一堂关于“缺席之本质”的讲座中途，你的影子背离了灯光，凑到你耳边，说出了你的名字。
# en: A student at a desk in a dim lecture hall, their shadow on the wall behind them turned the wrong way, leaning close to whisper.
scene [51c4bd] = 昏暗讲堂里的一个学生，身后墙上的影子朝向不对，正凑近低语。
# en: Banish it
opt.left.label [78332f] = 驱散它
# en: You speak the warding phrase. Your shadow snaps back into place, sulking. It does not speak again. You think.
opt.left.say.1 [9451ed] = 你念出防护咒语。影子啪地弹回原位，生着闷气。它没有再说话。你是这么想的。
# en: Answer it
opt.right.label [b623c8] = 回应它
# en: It tells you something about death you can't unlearn. The cold starts the next morning.
opt.right.say.1 [f3763b] = 它告诉了你一件关于死亡的事，你再也无法忘记。第二天早上，寒意开始了。
# en: It tells you where a lost book is shelved in the library. It is right. You decide not to wonder how it knew.
opt.right.say.2 [55a529] = 它告诉你图书馆里一本遗失的书放在哪里。它说对了。你决定不去想它是怎么知道的。

@event umbral_bone_mouse
# en: The Bone Mouse
title [ae9175] = 骨鼠
# en: Practical exercise: animate the skeleton of a field mouse. "Purely educational," the professor says, with a smile nobody trusts.
text [c20b3b] = 实践练习：让一具田鼠骨架活动起来。“纯属教学目的。”教授说，露出一个没人信得过的微笑。
# en: A tiny mouse skeleton on a silver tray, one bony paw twitching, students leaning away from it.
scene [e2a825] = 银托盘上一具小小的老鼠骨架，一只骨爪在抽动，学生们纷纷向后躲。
# en: Refuse on principle
opt.left.label [d08672] = 出于原则拒绝
# en: You write a short essay on why instead. The professor reads it with surprising attention.
opt.left.say.1 [ceeff8] = 你改写了一篇短文说明理由。教授读得出奇地认真。
# en: Do the exercise
opt.right.label [eb5633] = 完成练习
# en: The little skeleton stands up, washes its non-existent whiskers, and lies down again. Perfect control.
opt.right.say.1 [6bb00e] = 小骨架站起来，洗了洗并不存在的胡须，又躺了回去。控制得完美无缺。
# en: It gets up. It does not lie down again. It follows you back to your dormitory and sits on your pillow every night.
opt.right.say.2 [6046b9] = 它站了起来。然后再也没躺回去。它跟着你回了宿舍，每晚都坐在你的枕头上。

@event umbral_forbidden_notes
# en: Forbidden Notes
title [b392f3] = 禁忌笔记
# en: A fourth-year, Odile Varn, slides a battered notebook across the table. "My notes on the Restricted Section. I'm graduating. You look like you'd use them." A silver key is tucked in the spine.
text [bc2745] = 一个叫奥迪尔·瓦恩的四年级生把一本破旧的笔记本推过桌面。“我关于禁书区的笔记。我要毕业了。你看起来用得上。”书脊里夹着一把银钥匙。
# en: A battered notebook with a cracked leather cover being slid across a library table, a silver key tucked into its spine.
scene [9bca00] = 一本皮面开裂的破旧笔记本被推过图书馆的桌面，书脊里夹着一把银钥匙。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: The fourth-year shrugs and slides the notebook to the next student. You watch it go.
opt.left.say.1 [d26ee6] = 四年级生耸耸肩，把笔记本推给了下一个学生。你看着它被推走。
# en: Take the notebook
opt.right.label [beda2e] = 收下笔记本
# en: The notes are brilliant, half-mad and annotated in three colours of ink. The key is cold in your pocket: it opens the Restricted Section, the locked door at the back of the library, after hours.
opt.right.say.1 [402121] = 笔记精彩绝伦、半疯半癫，用三种颜色的墨水做了批注。那把钥匙在你口袋里冰凉：它能打开禁书区——图书馆后面那扇锁着的门，闭馆之后就能用。
